*
*   important hint:
*
*   Cycle time estimations can only be obtained by the KR C RCS Module
*   because the velocity profiles of the KR C controller can not be
*   emulated by the Robcad motion planner. The KRC motion planner
*   generates optimized velocity profiles depending on the robot position and
*   the current load.
*
*   This .e file contains neither joint velocities and joint accelerations
*   nor Cartesian velocities and Cartesian accelerations. We urgently recommend 
*   to use the KRC RCS Module for cycle time analysis.
*
*
*   A simulation is always based on assumptions with simplifications.
*   The KUKA RCS-Modules supports some of the 3D-Simulation functionalities.
*   A simulation with KUKA RCS Modules
*
*   - can not simulate the dynamic behaviours of a robot
*	(e.g. oscillation and vibrations)
*
*   - can not support the I/O functions of the robot. (restriction in RRS1)
*
*   - can not support external friction and inertia.
*	(e.g. gripper holding force, spot welding rebound etc.)
*
*   - can not simulate a flexible connection (eg.: cable package),
*     Some CAR-Tool supplied have tool for this functions.

